 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Lots of good ones out there, but one that never gets old is Yps the Secret Life of Objects at Yps Museum. Episodes are ten minutes each. Very, each object tells its own story, from thieving thieves in Egypt to being thrown out of a window in Rome. Five minutes is about the gold of Sardana, a woman from Bronze Age Phoenicia who made the king jealous. It's mind blowing. You' enjoy them on your commute or when you' waiting for the washing to finish.",
